course: dictionary
lesson: 9736
title: Sunny: more than the weather
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Sunny can mean bright with sunshine, but it can also describe a place or a person. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower.» The day and the flower are the clues: sunny means bright with sunshine.
explain: «Put a pondweed leaf in a glass of water on a sunny windowsill.» A windowsill is a place, so sunny here means a place that gets lots of sunshine. Always try your meaning in the sentence: does "bright with sunshine" still make sense? If yes, you have found it.
explain: Sunny can also describe a person. «Her sunny smile made everyone feel welcome.» A smile is not made of sunshine, so sunny means cheerful and happy. Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: Sunny means full of bright light from the Sun, with no or few clouds.
fact: A sunny place is one that gets a lot of sunshine.
fact: A sunny person is cheerful and happy, like «a sunny smile».
fact: Sunny days are warmer, and sunshine helps plants grow: tiny bubbles of oxygen rise from pondweed in the light.
fact: On sunny days, wear sunscreen, a hat and sunglasses, drink water, and find shade around midday, because the sun can be strong even in winter.
exercise: «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower.» What does sunny mean here? | Wet and windy | Dark and cloudy | Cheerful and happy | *Bright with sunshine and few clouds
exercise: «Put a pondweed leaf in a glass of water on a sunny windowsill.» Where should the glass go? | *On a windowsill where the sun shines | In the freezer | Under a pile of coats | In a dark cupboard
exercise: «Her sunny smile made everyone feel welcome.» What does sunny suggest about her? | *Cheerful and happy | Cold and wet | Tired and sleepy | Angry and loud
test: «Her sunny nature made the whole team smile.» Which meaning of sunny fits best? | *Cheerful and happy | Shady and cool | Full of bright sunshine | Cloudy and grey
test: A weather forecast shows a day as sunny. What symbol would you expect to see? | *A sun | A moon | A snowflake | A cloud with rain
exam: In a maths lesson, a chart asks «How many sunny days were there this month?» What does sunny mean in this question? | *Days with bright sunshine and few clouds | Days with no light at all | Days when people feel cheerful | Days with snow on the ground
